      "problem": "If $\\text{Var}[X]=18,$ calculate $\\text{Var}[\\frac{1}{3}X+1].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constants $a$ and $b,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+b]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=\\frac{1}{3}$ and $b=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[\\frac{1}{3}X+1] & ={(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot 18 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
